    <abstract id="aspace_17a5782b04cb0b387c2afc4947e47c5a" label="Abstract">Harlan Thompson was a writer of western novels for young people, sometimes published under the pseudonym, Stephen Holt; international president of P.E.N., 1958-59; won Boys' Clubs of America gold medal for <title render="italic">Prairie Colt</title> in 1948, and Commonwealth Club juvenile silver medal for <title render="italic">Spook</title>, <title render="italic">The Mustang</title> in 1957; other publications include <title render="italic">Wild Palomino</title> (1946), <title render="italic">Star Roan</title> (1952), and <title render="italic">Stormy</title> (1955). Collection consists of manuscripts and books by Thompson.</abstract>
